# q068 orderline_detail_crawl_dataset
# Intent: W4-1b FOLDED-CRAWL execution — the shape class NO corpus member covered
#   (a const-object member folded onto a co-located `?s ?p ?o` wildcard). The
#   ship-blocker returned ZERO triples for this shape (the folded wildcard emitted a
#   subject-only row, ?p/?o unbound), so this member's row-count parity
#   (native == virtual) catches that regression END-TO-END — exactly the gap that
#   nearly shipped. It also exercises the W4-1/W4-1b prune path: edw:lineNumber 1
#   folds as a star_constraint on the wildcard and pushes as an Iceberg scan filter,
#   and the ?ol->order/product ref POMs drive the parent-lookup (F-16 telemetry:
#   inspect whether FACT_ORDER is fully scanned vs bounded).
# BI lineage: the round-3b 071cd59f "show me everything about entity X" detail crawl.
# Predicates verified against enterprise-sf01-mapping.ttl — FactOrderLine: lineNumber
#   (LINE_NUMBER xsd:integer), class OrderLine; `?p`/`?o` range over all its triples.
# Determinism: an unordered crawl truncated by LIMIT -> hash_gate=rows_only (row-count
#   parity; the ship-blocker regression is 0 rows, which the count catches).
# Exec path: query_from() with FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main> (the deployed crawl path).
PREFIX edw: <http://ns.fluree.dev/edw#>
SELECT ?p ?o
FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main>
WHERE { ?ol a edw:OrderLine ; edw:lineNumber 1 . ?ol ?p ?o . }
LIMIT 200
